# MandalaOS Audit & Roadmap Walkthrough

This document summarizes the audit and research performed for the MandalaOS project and outlines the delivered roadmap.

## Accomplishments

### 1. Project Audit
I conducted a deep dive into the following core documents:
- [mandalaos.md](file:///home/lucas/Desktop/MandalaOS%20project/mandalaos.md): The central philosophical and technical specification.
- [mandala-glossary-plan.md](file:///home/lucas/Desktop/MandalaOS%20project/mandala-glossary-plan.md): The strategy for terminology management.
- [mandala-ui-prototype-brief.md](file:///home/lucas/Desktop/MandalaOS%20project/mandala-ui-prototype-brief.md): The requirements for the radial interface.
- [mandala-why-now.md](file:///home/lucas/Desktop/MandalaOS%20project/mandala-why-now.md): The market positioning and competitive analysis.

### 2. Feasibility Analysis
I evaluated three primary technical paths for building MandalaOS:
- **QubesOS**: Best for structural isolation but limited by the Xen hypervisor for the "Bindu" vision.
- **Linux + eBPF**: Most practical for behavioral monitoring and algorithm testing.
- **App Simulation**: Ideal for rapid UX iteration and vision alignment.

### 3. Delievered Roadmap
I produced a phased technical roadmap [mandalaos-feasibility-roadmap.md](file:///home/lucas/.gemini/antigravity/brain/fe5ed4b1-b5bc-4134-90d7-d78e4cea3538/mandalaos-feasibility-roadmap.md) which breaks the project into:
- **Simulation (Maya)**
- **Monitoring (Lakshmi)**
- **Ethical Enforcement (Yama)**
- **Language Compiler (SutraCode)**
- **Microkernel Core (Bindu)**

## Final Opinion
MandalaOS is a visionary project that addresses the "opacity crisis" in modern computing. By starting with a **simulation-first** approach and layering in **behavioral monitoring** on existing Linux/Qubes platforms, you can demonstrate the value of "Harmony" and "Dharma" before undertaking the massive engineering task of a custom microkernel.
